# Associate the policy with the network when you are ready:
#
# resource "google_compute_network_firewall_policy_association" "fwshift" {
#   name              = "fwshift-association"
#   project           = var.project
#   firewall_policy   = google_compute_network_firewall_policy.policy.id
#   attachment_target = "projects/PROJECT/global/networks/NETWORK"
# }

# Not written:
#   Web out: the source of the rule is in zone InternalZone, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind InternalZone with --zone-network; the destination of the rule is in zone ExternalZone, and a rule of Google Cloud names no zone: give the networks behind ExternalZone with --zone-networ
#   Social: references 'Facebook': object of type 'application-site'
#   Admins: references 'netadmins': access role whose networks and users are not in the export (add the output of 'show access-roles details-level full'); the source 'netadmins' holds members only its platform knows; a rule of Google Cloud names addresses
#   PLC access (plc-operators): source user match ad_group_PLC-Operators is not converted
#   PLC access (vendor-support): source user match ad_group_Vendor-Support is not converted
#   DMZ users: source user match known-user is not converted
#   Updates: schedule 'Work-Hours' is not converted; the rule would apply at all times; host name object .updates.example.com: the rules are written with addresses
#   Old rule: references 'lan-without-guests': object of type 'group-with-exclusion'; the source 'lan-without-guests' holds members only its platform knows; a rule of Google Cloud names addresses
#   Partners: not converted: VPN community match Partner-VPN
#   DMZ access / Ping from LAN: what it allows cannot be said by a rule of Google Cloud
